#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:0
msgid ""
"Switch Windows from Intel RST to AHCI so Ubuntu can install alongside it, "
"and repair Windows boot problems afterward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:8
msgid "Topics: Installation Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:12
msgid "Reconfigure Windows to use AHCI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:14
msgid ""
"If the Ubuntu installer detects RST, and Windows is installed on your "
"system, these steps enable Ubuntu to install side by side with Windows, "
"without any loss of data and functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:16
msgid ""
"To learn more about RST and its behavior with Ubuntu, see {ref}`intel-rst-"
"during-ubuntu-installation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:19
msgid "Back up your data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:21
msgid ""
"Any hard drive structure or configuration change, or installation of new "
"operating systems on a hard drive that already contains data might "
"potentially lead to a data loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:23
msgid ""
"Make sure that your personal data is safe. Even simply copying the important "
"files to an external drive minimizes the risk of data loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:26
msgid "Find the current controller mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:28
msgid "Open the Device Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:30
msgid ""
"Under {guilabel}`IDE ATA/ATAPI controllers`, verify which controller mode is "
"in use in Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:32
msgid ""
"If the controller mode is set to anything other than {guilabel}`Standard "
"SATA AHCI Controller`, you need to make a change that allows Windows to boot "
"safely in AHCI mode. This can be done using the Registry Editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:35
msgid "Change the controller mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:37
msgid ""
"Use the following steps to switch your Windows storage controller to AHCI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:39
msgid "Change registry keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:41
msgid "Start Registry Editor, and navigate to the following path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:43
msgid "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\iaStorV\\\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:47
msgid "![Regedit](/images/windows-ahci/Regedit.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:47
msgid "Regedit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:49
msgid ""
"In the right column, double-click the `Start` key, and change its value to "
"`0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:51
msgid ""
"Double-click the `iaStorV` entry in the left column to expand it and select "
"the `StartOverride` entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:53
msgid "In the right column, change the value of the key `0` to `0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:55
msgid "![Regedit override](/images/windows-ahci/Regedit-override-dword.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:55
#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:97
msgid "Regedit override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:57
msgid ""
"Repeat these changes for the following path in the Registry Editor, if the "
"path exists on your system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:59
msgid "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\storahci\\\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:63
msgid "Disable additional storage features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:65
msgid ""
"If your system uses BitLocker, disable it. See {ref}`turn-off-bitlocker-in-"
"windows`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:67
msgid ""
"If your system uses Intel Optane Memory, disable it. See [How to Disable "
"System Acceleration with Intel® Optane™ Memory](https://www.intel.com/"
"content/www/us/en/support/articles/000024626/memory-and-storage/intel-optane-"
"memory.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:69
msgid "Switch to safe boot mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:71
msgid ""
"Open the System Configuration app. You can find it by entering `msconfig` in "
"the Windows search menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:73
msgid ""
"On the {guilabel}`Boot` tab, enable {guilabel}`Safe boot` in the {guilabel}"
"`Boot options` frame. Confirm by clicking {guilabel}`OK`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:75
msgid "Change firmware settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:77
msgid "Reboot the system and start your computer’s firmware (BIOS or UEFI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:79
msgid ""
"Usually, you can access the firmware by pressing the {kbd}`F2` or {kbd}`Del` "
"key during the early boot sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:81
msgid "In the firmware menu, change the disk controller type to AHCI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:83
msgid ""
"The exact terminology and steps to manage the controller type in the "
"firmware depend on the implementation by the platform vendor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:85
msgid "Finish and verify the changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:87
msgid "Exit the firmware and let the system boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:89
msgid ""
"Windows enters safe mode and sets up the hardware using the temporarily "
"enabled drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:91
msgid ""
"After Windows starts, open the System Configuration app again and disable "
"{guilabel}`Safe boot`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:93
msgid "Check the controller mode in the Device Manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:95
msgid "It should read: {guilabel}`Standard SATA AHCI Controller`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:97
msgid "![Regedit override](/images/windows-ahci/Regedit-override.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:99
msgid "Reboot. Windows starts normally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:101
msgid "Troubleshooting boot problems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:103
msgid ""
"After making the necessary changes to enable Ubuntu to install side by side "
"with Windows, Windows might no longer boot. For instance, this might happen "
"if you made the firmware change without making the registry changes in "
"Windows. In this case, you need to recover your Windows installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:105
msgid ""
"![The INACCESSIBLE BOOT DEVICE error screen](/images/windows-ahci/"
"INACCESSIBLE-BOOT-DEVICE.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:105
msgid "The INACCESSIBLE BOOT DEVICE error screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:107
msgid ""
"You will most likely see a blue screen with a Stop code: `INACCESSIBLE BOOT "
"DEVICE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:109
msgid ""
"Windows attempts to restart and automatically diagnose and repair the boot-"
"related problems, but it will probably fail to complete the task itself. You "
"need to manually launch the command prompt from the recovery screen and fix "
"the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:111
msgid "Open the command prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:113
msgid ""
"On the screen that gives you the result of the Automatic Repair, click "
"{guilabel}`Advanced options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:115
msgid ""
"![The Automatic Repair screen](/images/windows-ahci/Automatic-repair.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:115
msgid "The Automatic Repair screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:117
msgid ""
"From the {guilabel}`Choose an option` screen, go to {menuselection}"
"`Troubleshoot --> Advanced options --> Command Prompt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:119
msgid ""
"![Automatic repair did not work](/images/windows-ahci/Automatic-repair-did-"
"not-work.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:119
msgid "Automatic repair did not work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:121
msgid "Diagnose the problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:123
msgid ""
"The Windows command prompt opens. Here, you can run commands to diagnose and "
"repair problems, including boot-related issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:125
msgid "![The command prompt](/images/windows-ahci/Windows-command-prompt.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:125
msgid "The command prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:127
msgid ""
"From the command prompt, run the disk partition tool to see and understand "
"the disk layout:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:129
msgid "diskpart\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:133
msgid "Display the list of volumes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:135
msgid "list volume\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:139
msgid ""
"Make sure the volume that contains Windows is correctly assigned the letter "
"`C:`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:141
msgid ""
"If the Windows volume isn't `C:`, you need to change this using the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:143
msgid "select volume [number]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:147
msgid "assign letter=[letter]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:151
msgid ""
"For example, a \"wrong\" volume might be assigned the letter `C:`. Select it "
"first, assign it a different letter (e.g. `F:` or `H:`), select the volume "
"that contains Windows, and then assign it the letter `C:`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:153
msgid ""
"![Disk partitioning example](/images/windows-ahci/windows-10-diskpart.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:153
msgid "Disk partitioning example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:155
msgid "Exit the `diskpart` utility:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:157
msgid "exit\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:161
msgid "Repair the problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:163
msgid "Run the `bcdedit repair` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:165
msgid "bcdedit /deletevalue {default} safeboot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:169
msgid "If the previous command does not work, try alternative commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:171
msgid "bcdedit /deletevalue {current} safeboot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:175
msgid "bcdedit /deletevalue safeboot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:179
msgid ""
"If the previous command completes successfully, exit the command prompt, the "
"Windows recovery console will restart, and Windows should load normally, "
"with the controller mode set to AHCI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:181
msgid ""
"If Windows does not start correctly, you can then manually recreate the boot "
"loader file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:183
msgid "Recreating the boot loader file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:185
msgid ""
"To this end, you need to access either the System partition or the EFI "
"partition on your computer. The Windows disk layout typically includes one "
"of these two configurations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:187
msgid ""
"A volume that contains Windows (`C:`) and a small hidden partition, usually "
"100MB in size called System partition, formatted as NTFS. It contains the "
"files needed to start (boot) Windows, as well as recovery tools to help you "
"diagnose and repair your system when it does not start correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:189
msgid ""
"On UEFI-based computers, a volume that contains Windows (`C:`) and a boot "
"partition (also called EFI), typically 256-512MB in size, formatted as "
"FAT32. This partition contains the files needed to start (boot) Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:191
msgid "You need to access the partition to make the necessary changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:193
msgid ""
"If you have already run the `diskpart` utility, you do not need to do "
"anything at this point, you only need to check the letter that is assigned "
"to this partition (e.g. letter `F:`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:195
msgid ""
"Assuming letter `F:` for the boot partition, use the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:197
msgid "Switch to the boot partition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:199
msgid "F:\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:203
msgid "cd boot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:207
msgid "Move the existing boot file aside:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:209
msgid "ren BCD BCD.bak\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:213
msgid "Create a new one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:215
msgid "bcdboot c:\\windows /l en-us /s f: /f ALL\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:219
msgid ""
"The `bcdboot` command initializes the system partition by using BCD files "
"from the `C:\\Windows` folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:221
msgid "The options used in the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:223
msgid "`/l en-us`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:224
msgid "Use the `en-us` locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:226
msgid "`/s f:`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:227
msgid "Target the system partition assigned letter `F:`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:229
msgid "`/f ALL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:230
msgid "Create boot files both for UEFI and BIOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:232
msgid ""
"Once the previous command completes, reboot. Windows should start normally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci.md:234
msgid ""
"You can now re-launch the Ubuntu installer and finish the side-by-side setup "
"of the two operating systems."
msgstr ""
